OVERHEAD CRANE HOIST & BRAKE SYSTEM
CAUSES OF FAILURE & PREVENTION

Main assembly:
  [Brake Assembly] -- electromagnetic DC/AC brake
  [Wire Rope Drum] -- wraps steel wire rope
  [Gearbox] -- reduces motor speed, increases torque
  [Motor] -- provides power to hoist

Load path:
  Drum --> Wire Rope --> Pulley Block --> Hook (safety latch)

FAILURE MODES
  worn_brake_lining     : lining wear reduces braking effectiveness
  hydraulic_failure     : leaks / pressure loss cut brake force and holding ability
  oil_contamination     : oil/grease on liner or drum drops friction
  overheating           : heat shortens insulation life, can fail brake or motor
  improper_adjustment   : wrong air gap or setting causes slip or drag

PREVENTIVE MEASURES
  INSPECT  : check lining, drum, rope; look for wear, damage, leaks, contamination
  TEST     : verify holding ability, release, emergency stop, load-holding
  MAINTAIN : keep clean and lubricated; set brake per manufacturer; replace worn parts promptly

Regular inspection + test + maintain = safer operation, longer life, less downtime.
